{"id": "en-p20-0001", "text": "The quickest fix is to bump the connection pool size and move on, since that is one config line. However, looking at the errors again, every timeout happens right after a schema migration, so the pool was never the bottleneck and we need to serialise the migrations instead.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 97, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "strong-phrase", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 48, "topic_id": "p20-db-pool-migration", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0002", "text": "我建议先把缓存层加上，这样查询压力立刻就降下来了，改动也小。然而，我仔细看了一遍日志，慢查询其实都集中在写入路径，缓存根本帮不上忙，我们得先解决写放大。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 30, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "strong-phrase", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 76, "topic_id": "p20-cache-write-amplify", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0003", "text": "Let us store the prices as floating point; it is simpler and the code reads cleaner for everyone. On second thought, rounding errors will accumulate across that many invoices, so integer cents are the only safe representation here.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 98, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "strong-phrase", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 38, "topic_id": "p20-money-float-cents", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0004", "text": "先按月份给这些数据建索引就够了，查询量并不大，没必要过度设计。话说回来，报表工具其实是按天聚合的，月索引完全命中不了查询，还是得老老实实建天粒度的索引。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 31, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "strong-phrase", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 76, "topic_id": "p20-index-粒度", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0005", "text": "We can just delete the legacy rows and backfill them from the replica later tonight. Wait — the replica is the one we are about to rebuild, so backfilling from it would copy the same corruption straight back in.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 85, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "interjection", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 39, "topic_id": "p20-legacy-rows-replica", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0006", "text": "这个参数默认值调大一点就能缓解抖动，先这么改吧，改动最小。等等，默认值一改，所有租户都会受影响，我们其实只想给那个大客户放宽，不能一刀切。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 29, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "interjection", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 69, "topic_id": "p20-参数抖动租户", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0007", "text": "The tests all pass locally, so I will merge the branch right away and tag a release. Hold on, CI runs on the older runtime where that API does not exist yet, so merging now would break the build for everyone.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 85, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "interjection", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 41, "topic_id": "p20-ci-runtime-api", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0008", "text": "把超时统一设成三十秒最简单，先全局改掉就好。等一下，批处理任务本来就要跑好几分钟，三十秒会把它们全部杀掉，这个值不能全局设。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 22, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "interjection", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 62, "topic_id": "p20-timeout-批处理", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0009", "text": "Switching to a message queue will decouple the services nicely and smooth out the traffic spikes. But the ordering guarantees we rely on would vanish, and billing cannot tolerate out-of-order events, so a queue is the wrong tool here.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 98, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 39, "topic_id": "p20-queue-ordering-billing", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0010", "text": "把这个模块拆成独立服务，团队就能各自发布了，听起来很理想。但拆出去以后每次调用都要走网络，这条链路的延迟预算根本放不下，还是留在进程内更合适。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 29, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 71, "topic_id": "p20-拆分服务延迟", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0011", "text": "We could cache the rendered page for a full minute to cut the database load dramatically. Yet the price shown there must track live inventory, and a stale minute would sell stock that we no longer have.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 90, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 37, "topic_id": "p20-page-cache-inventory", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0012", "text": "用正则来解析这些日志行是最快的办法，一行就能搞定。不过日志里嵌了 JSON，正则一遇到转义引号就崩，这种格式只能老老实实按 JSON 解析。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 25, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 67, "topic_id": "p20-日志正则json", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0013", "text": "So the plan is to read the config file synchronously at startup, which keeps the boot sequence simple. Actually, that is wrong — startup runs inside the event loop, and a blocking read there stalls every other service, so it has to be async.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 103, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 44, "topic_id": "p20-config-sync-async", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0014", "text": "我前面说这个接口是幂等的，客户端可以随便重试而不用担心。其实我说错了，它每次都会写一条审计记录，重试会产生重复条目，必须先加上去重键。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 28, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 67, "topic_id": "p20-接口幂等审计", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0015", "text": "Let me tell them to raise the memory limit and restart the worker, that usually buys us a few days. I realise now that the worker leaks a file handle per request, so more memory only delays the crash by an hour.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 100, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 42, "topic_id": "p20-worker-fd-leak", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0016", "text": "刚才我判断瓶颈在网络带宽上，建议直接加机器扩容。更正一下，压测显示网卡只用了三成，真正卡住的是磁盘随机读，加机器根本没用。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 24, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 61, "topic_id": "p20-瓶颈磁盘随机读", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0017", "text": "Storing the session in a signed cookie keeps the server stateless and simple to scale out. Then again, our logout must take effect immediately on every device, and a cookie cannot be revoked, so a server-side store wins after all.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 91, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "hedged-return", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 40, "topic_id": "p20-session-cookie-revoke", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0018", "text": "用乐观锁来处理并发写看起来挺合适，冲突时重试一下就好。话虽如此，热门商品的重试率会高得离谱，实际压测下大部分请求都要重试好几次，悲观锁反而更稳。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 27, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "hedged-return", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 72, "topic_id": "p20-乐观锁重试", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0019", "text": "Retrying the failed webhook three times should be enough to cover transient downstream outages. That said, the downstream deduplicates nothing, so a retry after a slow success duplicates the order every single time.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 96, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "hedged-return", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 33, "topic_id": "p20-webhook-retry-dedup", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0020", "text": "把这个字段做成可空就行，历史数据不用迁移，看着省事。不过想想还是不对，下游代码到处假设它非空，改成可空会静默产生空指针，得老老实实补默认值。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 26, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "hedged-return", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 70, "topic_id": "p20-字段可空迁移", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0021", "text": "Start the migration inside a maintenance window and keep an eye on the dashboards while it runs. Wait for the replication lag to drop below one second before you switch the traffic over to the new primary, and only then update the connection strings in every service that talks to it.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 51, "topic_id": "p20-wait-repl-lag", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "wait for", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0022", "text": "You can run these two cleanup steps in parallel to save time on the backup host, but wait until the lock file disappears before deleting the temporary directory, otherwise the workers will just recreate it and you will be back where you started.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 43, "topic_id": "p20-wait-lockfile", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "wait until", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0023", "text": "After you push the tag the pipeline needs a few minutes to build and publish the container image to the registry. Just wait for the green check to appear on the pull request page before you announce the release to the rest of the company.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 45, "topic_id": "p20-wait-ci-green", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "wait for", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0024", "text": "During the network handshake the client sends a SYN packet and the server answers with a SYN-ACK. The client must wait for the final ACK from the server before it starts sending any application data over that freshly opened connection.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 40, "topic_id": "p20-wait-handshake", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "wait for", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0025", "text": "The scheduler polls the job queue every five seconds for new work. Each worker should wait until it has successfully claimed a job before it opens a database connection, so that idle workers never hold connections open and starve the pool.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 41, "topic_id": "p20-wait-claim-job", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "wait until", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0026", "text": "This refactor is cleaner and easier to extend but it also requires noticeably more upfront work across the whole module. Both approaches are defensible on their merits, so let us weigh the tradeoffs carefully together before we commit to one of them.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 42, "topic_id": "p20-but-balanced-refactor", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "but", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0027", "text": "The library is small but well maintained, and the documentation is clear and always up to date. Overall it seems like a reasonable dependency to adopt for a project of this size, so I would not rule it out on principle.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 41, "topic_id": "p20-but-small-maintained", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "but", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0028", "text": "The synchronous API is easier to reason about but it blocks the calling thread, and the asynchronous one scales better but is much harder to debug when something goes wrong. Both are reasonable, so pick whichever style fits your existing team.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 41, "topic_id": "p20-but-sync-async", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "but", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0029", "text": "The new parser is a little faster but also noticeably stricter, rejecting any malformed input instead of quietly guessing at what was meant. That combination of speed and strictness is exactly what this ingestion pipeline needs.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 36, "topic_id": "p20-but-faster-stricter", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "but", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0030", "text": "The main service is written in Go and deployed as a single static binary with no external runtime. However, there is also a small Python helper in the same repository that is used only by the offline reporting job once a night.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 42, "topic_id": "p20-however-python-helper", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "however", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0031", "text": "Install the command line tool from your distribution package manager to get the stable release quickly. However, you can also build it from source if you need a feature that has not shipped in a tagged release yet.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 38, "topic_id": "p20-however-build-source", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "however", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0032", "text": "We can shard the events table by user id, which spreads the write load evenly across all the nodes. However, we could equally shard it by tenant instead; both keys distribute the traffic well and neither choice is obviously wrong.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 40, "topic_id": "p20-however-shard-key", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "however", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0033", "text": "The default timeout is thirty seconds, which suits the interactive request path nicely. However, the batch endpoints override that value to ten minutes, so they happen to be covered by the very same configuration file.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 35, "topic_id": "p20-however-batch-timeout", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "however", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0034", "text": "The helper function is actually quite simple: it just normalises the incoming path and returns it unchanged whenever the path is already absolute, so it is very cheap to call in a tight loop.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 34, "topic_id": "p20-actually-simple-helper", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "actually", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0035", "text": "The cache is actually shared across all of the worker threads, so you do not need to warm it up separately in each thread. One warm-up during startup is quite enough to serve the whole pool efficiently.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 37, "topic_id": "p20-actually-shared-cache", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "actually", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0036", "text": "That flag is actually deprecated and will be removed in the next major release, so brand new code should avoid it entirely. Use the replacement option that the documentation now recommends in every example.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 34, "topic_id": "p20-actually-deprecated-flag", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "actually", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0037", "text": "GraphQL gives clients exactly the fields they ask for and avoids the over-fetching that plagues REST endpoints. That said, its flexible queries also make response caching a good deal more complex to get right in practice.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 36, "topic_id": "p20-said-graphql-cache", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "that said", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0038", "text": "Moving to a monorepo simplifies cross-package dependency management and keeps versioning consistent across teams. Having said that, it also means every CI run now has to build the whole tree, which is measurably slower.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 34, "topic_id": "p20-said-monorepo-ci", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "having said that", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0039", "text": "Rust gives us memory safety without a garbage collector pause, which is great for latency-sensitive services. That said, the borrow checker does raise the learning curve for anyone joining the team from a scripting background.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 35, "topic_id": "p20-said-rust-curve", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "that said", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0040", "text": "First, install the project dependencies into a clean virtual environment. Second, run the database migration against a recent copy of production data. Third, start the server and check that the health endpoint returns ok before you point any traffic at it.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 41, "topic_id": "p20-fs-install-steps", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "first", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0041", "text": "There are two good reasons to prefer a queue here: first, it absorbs sudden traffic bursts, and second, it lets us retry failed deliveries independently without ever blocking the producer that created them.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 33, "topic_id": "p20-fs-two-reasons", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "first", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0042", "text": "There are three layers in this system: first the edge gateway, second the internal service mesh, and third the application itself. Each of those layers adds its own latency and its own distinct set of failure modes.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 37, "topic_id": "p20-fs-three-layers", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "first", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0043", "text": "First we profile the slow endpoint to find the hot loop that is burning the cycles. Second we replace the nested query with a single join. Third we add a regression test so that the same problem cannot quietly come back.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 41, "topic_id": "p20-fs-profile-fix", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "first", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0044", "text": "This approach is probably the safest choice available to us here; it is a little slower, but it reliably avoids the race condition we have been fighting for two full sprints now. I would go with it again.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 38, "topic_id": "p20-hed-safest-choice", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "probably", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0045", "text": "It might not be the most elegant solution on the whiteboard, yet it is dependable and easy for the whole team to maintain, and in this particular codebase that matters a good deal more than elegance.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 36, "topic_id": "p20-hed-dependable", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "yet", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0046", "text": "The migration will likely take about ten minutes on the largest tenants, but it is safe to run fully online because it only adds columns and never rewrites any of the existing rows in place.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 35, "topic_id": "p20-hed-online-migration", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "likely", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0047", "text": "You should perhaps start with the smaller tables first in order to build confidence, but the very same script will work on the biggest one when you are finally ready to commit to making that change.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 36, "topic_id": "p20-hed-small-tables", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "perhaps", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0048", "text": "In short, the bottleneck is the database, and every measurement we took over the last hour points that way. To fix it we should add the missing composite index and tune the slow query that keeps showing up in the profile.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 41, "topic_id": "p20-sum-bottleneck-db", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "in short", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0049", "text": "To summarise, we recommend the incremental migration over the risky big-bang cutover we discussed earlier. It keeps the risk contained and, as shown above, still satisfies every requirement that we listed at the start.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 34, "topic_id": "p20-sum-incremental", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "to summarise", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0050", "text": "So, to wrap up: keep the current architecture as it is, add the metrics we discussed, and revisit the split only if the load genuinely doubles. Nothing else really needs to change right now.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 34, "topic_id": "p20-sum-keep-architecture", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "to wrap up", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0051", "text": "The parser is fast, yet it remains strict, rejecting any malformed line instead of quietly guessing at the intent. That combination of raw speed and strictness is exactly what we want for this ingest path.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 35, "topic_id": "p20-yet-strict-parser", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "yet", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0052", "text": "The migration is reversible, yet it is still worth testing on a fresh snapshot of production first. Caution and reversibility are not mutually exclusive, and we can easily have both with a little planning.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 34, "topic_id": "p20-yet-reversible-test", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "yet", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0053", "text": "The retry policy uses exponential backoff with full jitter, capped at thirty seconds between attempts. This keeps the whole fleet from retrying in lockstep after a brief outage finally comes to an end.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 33, "topic_id": "p20-plain-backoff", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0054", "text": "Bcrypt is intentionally slow, and that slowness is the entire point of choosing it: it makes brute-forcing a stolen password database expensive for whoever ends up holding the hashes afterwards.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 30, "topic_id": "p20-plain-bcrypt", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0055", "text": "The index should cover the three columns in the order they appear in the where clause, so the query planner can seek directly instead of scanning the whole table on every single incoming request.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 34, "topic_id": "p20-plain-index-order", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0056", "text": "Feature flags let us ship the code dark and then turn it on for one tenant at a time, which means a rollback is just a config change rather than a full redeploy, and that is far faster.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 38, "topic_id": "p20-plain-feature-flags", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0057", "text": "先把备份完整跑完再动手，耐心等待所有分片都同步完成，确认主从之间没有任何延迟之后，再切换到新的集群上去。", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 52, "topic_id": "p20-等待分片同步", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "等待", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0058", "text": "这个脚本会阻塞在这一行，它会一直等待子进程彻底结束，直到收到明确的退出码之后才会继续往下执行后面的步骤。", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 52, "topic_id": "p20-等待子进程", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "等待", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0059", "text": "发布之后流水线还需要跑好几分钟才能出结果，你就安静地等待那个绿色的勾出现在合并请求页面上，然后再动手也不迟。", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 54, "topic_id": "p20-等待流水线绿勾", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "等待", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-p20-0060", "text": "这个项目需要的第三方依赖有 numpy、pandas、scikit-learn 等，把它们全部写进 requirements 文件里，方便在任何机器上一键重建环境。", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 5, "topic_id": "p20-等依赖列表", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "等", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-p20-0061", "text": "常见的错误码像 400、401、404、500 等都应该在网关层做统一映射和记录，前端只需要关心封装好的业务错误码就够了。", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 59, "topic_id": "p20-等错误码列表", "source_model": "deepseek-flash", "peer_session": "08176c26-e91e-46dc-b216-a61935c71231", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "等", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
